challenge-edit-label-hide-classmates-responses = Don't show classmates' responses after completing a challenge (for challenges with unique solutions).
challenge-edit-label-solid-color = Empty Solid Color
challenge-edit-label-student-skips-response = Student doesn't need to respond to their own challenge.
challenge-edit-message-make-challenge = Add screen(s) for students to create their challenge.
challenge-edit-message-solve-challenge = Add a screen for students to solve the challenge.
challenge-edit-narration-add-make-screen = Add a "Make" screen to Challenge Creator
challenge-edit-narration-add-solve-screen = Add a "Solve" screen to Challenge Creator
challenge-edit-narration-create-screens-list = "Make the challenge" subscreens
challenge-edit-narration-moved-screen-to-cc = Moved screen { $title } from main lesson to Challenge Creator
challenge-edit-narration-solve-screens-list = "Solve the challenge" subscreens
challenge-edit-narration-subscreen-reordered-make = Challenge Creator subscreen moved to position { $position } in the "Make" screens list.
challenge-edit-narration-subscreen-reordered-solve = Challenge Creator subscreen moved to the "Solve" screens list.
challenge-playground-button-delete-challenge = Delete Challenge
challenge-playground-button-edit-response = Edit Response
challenge-playground-button-make-my-challenge = Make My Challenge
challenge-playground-button-my-response = My Response
challenge-playground-button-resume-editing = Resume Editing My Challenge
challenge-playground-button-submit-challenge = Submit Challenge
challenge-playground-button-submit-response = Submit Response
challenge-playground-heading-gallery = Class Gallery
challenge-playground-heading-my-challenge = My Challenge
challenge-playground-heading-other-students = Other Students' Challenges
challenge-playground-label-completed-many = { $count } students completed
challenge-playground-label-completed-one = 1 student completed
challenge-playground-label-creator = Creator
challenge-playground-label-submitted = Submitted
challenge-playground-message-no-other-responses = No other responses yet. Check back later!
challenge-playground-message-no-responses = No responses yet. Check back later!
challenge-playground-message-no-solve-screen = No Solve screen
challenge-playground-message-waiting = Waiting for challenges from your classmates . . .
challenge-playground-narration-thumbnail-challenge = Challenge
challenge-playground-narration-thumbnail-response = Response
challenge-playground-prompt-confirm-delete = Are you sure you want to delete your challenge?
challenge-playground-title-delete-challenge = Delete Challenge
cl-docs-button-join-discussion = Join the discussion!
cl-docs-button-show-deprecated = Show Deprecated
cl-docs-button-show-internal = Show Internal
cl-docs-button-try-it = Try It
cl-docs-button-try-it-preview = Preview
cl-docs-description-action-button-capture =
    Sets a variable you want to capture every time the action button is pressed.
    (Retrieve the history of that variable later using the history source.)
cl-docs-description-action-button-disabled =
    Sets a Boolean that determines when the action button is disabled or enabled.
    (When it's disabled, we gray out the button and make it unpressable.)
cl-docs-description-action-button-label = Sets the text to show on the button. Keep it short.
cl-docs-description-action-button-press-count = Gets the number of times the action button has been pressed.
cl-docs-description-action-button-reset-label = Sets the link text we'll show that lets the student reset the action button.
cl-docs-description-action-button-reset-style = Sets the button style when in "reset" state. Use "link" for our standard link or "white" for button styling on a dark background.
cl-docs-description-action-button-style = Sets the button style. Use "default" for our standard plum style. Other options are "red" for a warning or for a confirmatory second click, "white" for a secondary click on a dark background, and "link" for our standard link.
cl-docs-description-action-button-time-since-press =
    Gets the seconds (plus milliseconds) since the "Submit" button was pressed. It
    resets to zero if the "reset" link is pressed, or if a component on the same
    page is focused or edited. By default, it runs to 10 seconds and then stops.
    Increase that time by passing a parameter, as in timeSincePress(20).
cl-docs-description-ai-query-input = Input query for an AI chat request.
cl-docs-description-ai-query-output = AI chat response.
cl-docs-description-annotation-arrow = Renders an arrow annotation from a start location to an end location.
cl-docs-description-annotation-label = Renders a label annotation around the target location.
cl-docs-description-annotation-lasso = Renders a lasso annotation around the target location.
cl-docs-description-annotation-line = Renders a line annotation from a start location to an end location.
cl-docs-description-annotation-reset-on-change = Specify a string value. If that value changes, the animation timer resets.
cl-docs-description-annotation-timer = Starts timer after being triggered, renders nothing.
cl-docs-description-annotation-timer-since-triggered = Returns running time, once relevant annotation timer has been triggered.
cl-docs-description-button-history = Gets the history of a variable that was defined using the "capture" sink.
cl-docs-description-button-last-value = Gets the last value captured for a variable that was defined using the "capture" sink.
cl-docs-description-button-submit-count = Gets the number of times the input has been submitted.
cl-docs-description-calculatorState-source = Gets the full state of a graph. Pass this, for example, into the graphLayer method.
cl-docs-description-cardsort-matches-key =
    Returns whether response matches the answer key. If no answer key is provided,
    returns false.
cl-docs-description-cardsort-total-cards = Number of cards in the Card Sort.
cl-docs-description-cardsort-total-correct =
    Number of cards correctly sorted according to the answer key Notes: (1) Cards
    that are supposed to be on their own are marked correct when on their own. (2)
    Cards correctly sorted into an incomplete group count as correct. (3) Cards in
    a group where any card is wrong are all counted as wrong.
cl-docs-description-challenge-background = Specify a thumbnail image for the challenge.
cl-docs-description-challenge-bounds = Set the bounds of the challengeBackground.
cl-docs-description-challenge-prevent-challenge-creation-reason =
    Has the challenge creator correctly set up their challenge? Warning if not,
    empty string if so.
cl-docs-description-challenge-prevent-submission-reason =
    Can the student submit this challenge? Provide an error message if not, empty
    string if so.
cl-docs-description-challenge-repsonse-bounds = Set the bounds of the responseBackground.
cl-docs-description-challenge-response-background = Specify a thumbnail image for the response.
cl-docs-description-challenge-response-text = Specify text to display on the thumbnail of the challenge or the response.
cl-docs-description-challenge-text = Specify text to display on the thumbnail of the challenge or the response.
cl-docs-description-correctness-correct =
    Sets a Boolean value that determines whether or not a gray checkmark is
    displayed for the student's screen in the dashboard's summary view.
cl-docs-description-correctness-read-only =
    Sets a Boolean value that determines whether or not a component will be ignored
    when determining a screen's correctness. If all components have a readOnly
    value of "true," we display a dash for the student's screen in the dashboard's
    summary view, indicating teachers can focus their efforts elsewhere.
cl-docs-description-correctness-warning =
    Sets a string that is displayed as a tooltip in the teacher dashboard attached
    to a warning icon.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-capture =
    Sets a variable you want to capture every time the expression input is
    submitted. (Often times this is the numeric value of the expression input.)
    Retrieve the history of that variable later using the history source.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-clear-on-reset = If true, when the user goes to edit their expression, we'll clear the prior one.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-disable-edit = Disables editing the expression.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-disable-evaluation = Never show evaluated user input on student side.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-error-message =
    An error to show to the student. Note: This will not show up in the teacher
    dashboard. (Use the "warning" sink to show warnings to the teacher.)
cl-docs-description-expression-input-explain-content = Content of the "explain" text box.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-explain-prompt =
    Sets a string that replaces the generic "Explain your thinking" prompt in the
    text input when students are asked to explain their answer.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-initial-latex = Sets the initial value of the expression input. Should be a valid LaTeX string.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-initial-text =
    Sets the initial value of the text input when students are asked to explain
    their thinking.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-latex =
    Gets the LaTeX string of the input, which is useful for importing into the
    graphing calculator, the note, and other components.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-numeric-value =
    Gets the evaluated value of an expression input. For example, "2+2" will return
    the number 4.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-placeholder-latex = Sets the placeholder of the input. Should be a valid LaTeX string.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-prompt-aria-label = Sets the aria label that will prompt the expression input.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-reset-label = Specify a label for the reset link.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-show-classmates =
    Overrides the "show classmates' responses" checkbox, and lets you use that
    feature even when it's not at the end of a column.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-show-explain = Should we ask students to explain their answer?
cl-docs-description-expression-input-show-submit =
    When true, force show submit button. When false, force hide submit button,
    unless a source relies on it.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-submit-disabled =
    Disable the submit button. Note: Even if set to false, the input button will be
    disabled if the input is empty.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-submit-label = Specify a label for the submit button.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-submitted =
    Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the expression input has
    been submitted.
cl-docs-description-expression-input-suffix =
    Adds a suffix to everything entered by the student. Recommended for inputs that
    expect a certain unit (e.g., ft. or %).
cl-docs-description-expression-input-time-since-submit =
    Gets the seconds (plus milliseconds) since the the expression input was
    submitted. It resets to zero if the student focuses into the input again.
    Increase that time by passing a parameter, as in timeSincePress(20).
cl-docs-description-graph-animation-duration =
    Adds an animation playhead on top of the graph as if it were a video. This
    sets the duration for the animation. A non-positive value hides the playhead.
    Note: Only works with graph exhibits.
cl-docs-description-graph-animation-keyboard-step =
    Sets the amount of time (in seconds) that an animation moves when its scrubber
    is adjusted with the arrow keys. If not specified, the scrubber moves in
    increments of 1 second. Note: Only works with graph exhibits.
cl-docs-description-graph-animation-time =
    Gets the position of the animation playhead. Use in conjunction with
    animationDuration.
cl-docs-description-graph-audiotrace-reverse =
    Specifies whether expressions are traversed in reverse order when audio trace
    is active. This behavior may be desired in situations where the curves you wish
    a student to examine are declared at the end of the calculator's expression
    list so that they appear in the foreground.
cl-docs-description-graph-background = Sets the background layer of the graph.
cl-docs-description-graph-bounds-sink =
    Sets the bounds of the graph. Commonly used in combination with the
    "background" sink. This overrides user interaction, so we caution against using
    it with fullscreen graphs.
cl-docs-description-graph-bounds-source = Gets the bounds of a graph component.
cl-docs-description-graph-expression-sink =
    Sets a variable in the calculator to an expression with the provided latex.
    This will override any existing definitions of that variable. The first parameter
    is the name of the variable or function to be defined. The optional additional parameters
    specify the symbols that the latex expression is allowed to reference. (By default,
    it will not be allowed to reference any existing variables or functions in the calculator.)
cl-docs-description-graph-has-response =
    Sets a Boolean value that determines whether to treat the component as having
    a response.  Setting this to "true" means that the component will be considered
    when determining a screen's correctness, and will be shown on the Teacher view
    of the dashboard.
cl-docs-description-graph-is-animating =
    Tells whether the animation is running.
    Use in conjunction with animationDuration.
cl-docs-description-graph-label-latex = Gets the inner latex content from a point label based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-graph-label-numeric-value = Evaluates to content of a point label based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-graph-label-text = Gets the content from a point label based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-graph-narration =
    Text that screen readers will read aloud. Similar to image alt text, narration
    can be used to describe a graph or sketch. Example: narration: "The
    graph shows a plot of time studied (in hours) on the x-axis and test scores on
    the y-axis." You can include multiple narrations for a graph to separate
    pieces of information from one another. Example: narration(1): "A description of
    the graph's main characteristics would go here." narration(2): "The line does
    not pass through all of the points." In the above example, narration(2) could
    change as the student interacts with the activity without needing to modify
    the graph description in narration(1). Separating narrations also minimizes the
    amount of text a screen reader needs to speak.
cl-docs-description-graph-number-list-sink =
    Sets a variable in the calculator to the contents of a list. This will override
    any existing definitions of that variable.
cl-docs-description-graph-number-list-source = Gets the list of numbers that was assigned to the variable in the graph.
cl-docs-description-graph-number-sink =
    Sets the value of a variable in the calculator. This will override any existing
    definitions of that variable.
cl-docs-description-graph-number-source = Gets the numerical value of a variable in the graph.
cl-docs-description-graph-point-location =
    Gets a location for a point on the graph to be used with feedback annotations.
    This takes a point name as the first argument and optional width and height arguments (in math space).
    If no width or height params then a default location size will be used and if only a
    width is supplied then the height will be set to the supplied width.
cl-docs-description-graph-raw-expression =
    Adds an expression that's exactly the latex provided. Warning: use this with
    caution! It's very brittle.
cl-docs-description-graph-raw-expression-color =
    Sets color for an expression, to be used in parallel with rawExpression. Note:
    this will only work if there is a rawExpression with the same identifier.
    Warning: use this with caution!!! It\`s very brittle.
cl-docs-description-graph-raw-expression-hidden =
    Sets the hidden property for an expression, to be used in parallel with
    rawExpression. Note: this will only work if there is a rawExpression with the
    same identifier. Warning: use this with caution!!! It's very brittle.
cl-docs-description-graph-raw-expression-point-label =
    Sets a label for a point. This only works for points defined like A=(1,2), and
    the identifier needs to match the name given to the point (A in this case).
    Takes a string. The label next to the point exactly matches the provided
    string, so the label is turned off if the empty string is provided.
cl-docs-description-graph-raw-expression-style =
    Sets the style property for an expression, to be used in parallel with
    rawExpression. Note: this will only work if there is a rawExpression with the
    same identifier. For lines, options are: "SOLID", "DOTTED", and "DASHED". For
    points, options are "POINT", "OPEN", and "CROSS". Warning: use this with
    caution!!! It's very brittle.
cl-docs-description-graph-save-on-change = Specify a string value. If that value changes, the component saves its state.
cl-docs-description-graph-show-reset-button = If this is a geometry component, controls the presence of the reset button.
cl-docs-description-graph-trace =
    Allows tracing curves to inspect coordinates and shows point coordinates when
    clicked.
cl-docs-description-graph-x-axis-label =
    Sets the string we display along the x-axis. This overrides any user
    interaction, so we caution against using it with fullscreen graphs.
cl-docs-description-graph-xmax = Sets xmax for the graph (all four bounds must be set to take effect)
cl-docs-description-graph-xmin = Sets xmin for the graph (all four bounds must be set to take effect)
cl-docs-description-graph-y-axis-label =
    Sets the string we display along the y-axis. This overrides any user
    interaction, so we caution against using it with fullscreen graphs.
cl-docs-description-graph-ymax = Sets ymax for the graph (all four bounds must be set to take effect)
cl-docs-description-graph-ymin = Sets ymin for the graph (all four bounds must be set to take effect)
cl-docs-description-hidden = When true, this component will not be shown to students.
cl-docs-description-image-alt-text =
    Sets the string which will be read by screen reading software. Only useful in
    conjnuction with internalImagePath. Use altText input on the component in other
    cases.
cl-docs-description-image-internal-image-path =
    Hash for an image hosted at https://uploads.desmos.com/activitybuilder/ (just
    what follows the hash)
cl-docs-description-inline-dropdown-choice-content = Gets the content of the choice at the given index, starting with 1.
cl-docs-description-inline-dropdown-disable-edit = Disables editing the dropdown.
cl-docs-description-inline-dropdown-is-selected =
    Gets a Boolean that describes whether or not a particular inline dropdown
    option has been selected, given the index of that option, starting with 1.
cl-docs-description-inline-location =
    Gets a location for an inline math or dropdown in the note to be used with feedback annotations.
    This takes an inline name as the first argument.
cl-docs-description-inline-math-has-focus =
    Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the student has focus on a
    particular inline math node.
cl-docs-description-lib-and =
    Takes two booleans and returns true if both are true. Use like "when ___ and
    ___"
cl-docs-description-lib-angle-of-line = Returns the angle an xyLine object makes with the x-axis, measured in radians.
cl-docs-description-lib-annotations = Annotations that can be attached to annotated feedback.
cl-docs-description-lib-bounds-getter = Get the { $name } property from the bounds object
cl-docs-description-lib-bounds-right = Get the right property from the bounds object
cl-docs-description-lib-bounds-square =
    Force the bounds to have a square aspect ratio, while preserving the provided
    edge.
cl-docs-description-lib-bounds-stretch = Show the bounds exactly, while allowing the aspect ratio to be non-square.
cl-docs-description-lib-bounds-top = Get the top property from the bounds object
cl-docs-description-lib-button-styles =
    Available styles for a button. "default" is our standard blue button. "red" is
    our standard red button. "link" is a button that looks like a link
cl-docs-description-lib-color-list = make a list of colors, e.g. for use in setting available colors in sketch
cl-docs-description-lib-conic = Create a new conic object from the provided latex string.
cl-docs-description-lib-conic-coefficients = Get the 3x3 coefficient matrix of a conic where each row represents x terms and each column represents y terms.
cl-docs-description-lib-count-number-usage =
    Counts numeric constants in a latex string. countNumberUsage(latex) counts all
    numbers, or if you provide a specific number as an argument, only that number
    specifically will be counted
cl-docs-description-lib-count-plus-minus = Takes a latex expression and returns the count of \xB1 instances in the expression.
cl-docs-description-lib-difference-function =
    simpleFunction representing for (lhs) - (rhs) of an equation. Useful for
    setting equal to zero to test or plot
cl-docs-description-lib-elementAt = Takes a List and an index, and returns the element of the list at that index (starts with 1)
cl-docs-description-lib-equation-lhs = Latex string for left-hand side of equation
cl-docs-description-lib-equation-rhs = Latex string for right-hand side of equation
cl-docs-description-lib-evaluation-frame = Creates a frame to store functions and variables for future evaluation.
cl-docs-description-lib-first-defined-value =
    Takes multiple arguments, all of the same type, and returns the first that's
    valid. Use, for example as "a = firstDefinedValue(exp1.numericValue, 2)". That
    will return 2 until exp.numericValue is valid.
cl-docs-description-lib-format-latex = Takes latex equations and expressions and applies a small set of simplification rules to format the equations and expressions nicely.
cl-docs-description-lib-frame-define = Define a function or assign a number value to a variable for future evaluation in a frame.
cl-docs-description-lib-frame-evaluate = Get the numeric value of an expression within a frame.
cl-docs-description-lib-get-horizontal-parabola = Returns a parabola object if the conic is a parabola aligned to the x axis.
cl-docs-description-lib-get-vertical-parabola = Returns a parabola object if the conic is a parabola aligned to the y axis.
cl-docs-description-lib-graph-layer = Create a layer from a graph. Use it like graphLayer(g.calculatorState)
cl-docs-description-lib-inequality-difference-function =
    simpleFunction representing for (greater side) - (lesser side) of an equation.
    Useful for setting equal to zero to test or plot, with f(x,y)>0
cl-docs-description-lib-inequality-is-left-greater =
    Which way does the inequality point? True for "greater than" and "greater than
    or equal to"
cl-docs-description-lib-inequality-isStrict = True for strict inequality, False for non-strict inequality
cl-docs-description-lib-inequality-lhs = Latex string for lef-hand side of inequality
cl-docs-description-lib-inequality-rhs = Latex string for right-hand side of inequality
cl-docs-description-lib-is-blank = Takes a string and returns a boolean of whether it's the empty string.
cl-docs-description-lib-is-defined =
    Takes any type and returns a boolean for if it's defined. For example, use with
    the numericValue of an expression input.
cl-docs-description-lib-is-line-horizontal =
    Returns a Boolean value given an xyLine object that indicates whether or not
    the line is horizontal.
cl-docs-description-lib-is-line-vertical =
    Returns a Boolean value given an xyLine object that indicates whether or not
    the line is vertical.
cl-docs-description-lib-is-undefined =
    Takes any type and returns a boolean for if it's undefined. For example, use
    with the numericValue of an expression input.
cl-docs-description-lib-layer-stack = Create a stack of layers from other layers.
cl-docs-description-lib-length = Takes a List and returns its length as a number.
cl-docs-description-lib-make-bounds =
    Create a bounds object given left, right, bottom, top. These bounds will have
    non-square axis, meaning that when applied to a graph/sketch entity, the entity
    will be stretched to show exactly these bounds.
cl-docs-description-lib-math-expression = evaluate function with given arguments
cl-docs-description-lib-max = Takes a numberList and returns its largest value as a number.
cl-docs-description-lib-merge-sketches = Create a sketch from other sketches.
cl-docs-description-lib-min = Takes a numberList and returns its smallest value as a number.
cl-docs-description-lib-not = Takes a boolean and returns its opposite. Use like "when not(___)"
cl-docs-description-lib-numeric-value =
    Takes a latex string, and evaluates it to a number, if possible. Returns NaN if
    it fails
cl-docs-description-lib-or =
    Takes two booleans and returns true if either one is true. Use like "when ___
    or ___"
cl-docs-description-lib-ordered-pair-x = Latex string for first element of pair
cl-docs-description-lib-ordered-pair-y = Latex string for second element of pair
cl-docs-description-lib-palette-color-getter = The color { $name } used in the Desmos calculator.
cl-docs-description-lib-palette-colors = A convenient way to get at colors used by the Desmos calculator.
cl-docs-description-lib-parabola-coefficients = Get the 3x3 coefficient matrix of a parabola where each row represents x terms and each column represents y terms.
cl-docs-description-lib-parabola-is-horizontal = Returns true if the parabola is aligned to the x axis.
cl-docs-description-lib-parabola-is-vertical = Returns true if the parabola is aligned to the y axis.
cl-docs-description-lib-parse-equation = Takes a latex string, e.g. "2x+y=1" - and returns an equation object
cl-docs-description-lib-parse-inequality =
    Takes a latex string, e.g. "2x+y>1" - and returns an inequality object. Does
    not recognize compound inequalities.
cl-docs-description-lib-parse-ordered-pair =
    Takes a latex string - e.g. "(a,2)" - and returns a coordinate pair - e.g. x:
    "a", y: "2".
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-allow-negative-terms =
    Allows for negatives terms in a sum. The latex is modified to turn subtraction
    into addition of negative terms.
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-allow-parens =
    Allow parentheses in this and child patterns (default, unless there is a reject
    above this point)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-any-of = Match one of several pattern options
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-arg-n = The pattern corresponding to argument { $termNumber } in the function
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-base = Base of the exponent
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator = Pattern to parse comparators e.g. x>2
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-chain = Pattern to parse comparator chains e.g. 5>x>2
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-chain-n = The number of comparators in the comparator chain
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-chain-nth = The nth comparator in a comparator chain e.g. nth(1) for 5>x>2 is 5>x
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-lhs = Latex string for left-hand side of a comparator
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-rhs = Latex string for right-hand side of a comparator
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-comparator-symbol = Latex string for symbol in a comparator e.g. ">" for x>2
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-contains = Pattern to match any expression that contains given terms somewhere within it
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-degree = degree of this nth root
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-denominator = denominator of the fraction
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-difference = Pattern to parse a difference (subtraction)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-dividend = Dividend of the division
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-division = Pattern to parse a division
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-divisor = Divisor of the division
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-exponent = Pattern to parse an exponent
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-expression = Pattern to match any latex expression
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-fraction = Pattern to parse a fraction
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-function-call = Pattern to parse function calls e.g. f(x)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-function-call-identifier = The identifier of the function e.g. "f" in f(x)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-function-call-n = The number of arguments called in the function
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-function-call-nth = The nth argument in the function e.g. nth(1) for f(x) is x
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-integer = Pattern to parse a number, restricted to integers
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-literal = Pattern to parse a literal latex string
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-match-latex = get the latex that matches this part of the pattern
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-matches = Does the provided latex match this pattern?
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-minuend = minuend of the difference (a, in a-b)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-mixed-number = Pattern for a mixed number (like 1 1/2)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-mixed-number-denominator = Denominator of fraction portion of mixed number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-mixed-number-numerator = Numerator of fraction portion of mixed number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-mixed-number-numeric-value = Numeric value of this mixed number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-mixed-number-whole = Whole number portion of mixed number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-negated = expression which is negated
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-negative = Pattern to match an expression with a negative-sign in front of it
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-number = Pattern to parse a number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-number-numeric-value = Numeric value of this number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-numerator = numerator of the fraction
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-optional = Allow a term in a sum or product to repeat n times
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-parse =
    Parse latex string and return an a PatternMatch object that matches the
    structure of this pattern
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-power = The exponent that the base is raised to
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-product = Pattern to parse product of terms
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-radical = Pattern to parse a radical
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-radicand = value under the radical sign
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-reject-negative-terms = Disallows subtraction in a sum expression.
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-reject-parens = Disallow parentheses in this and child patterns
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-repeat = Allow a term in a sum or product to repeat n times
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-repeated-n = Number of times this term repeated
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-repeated-nth = nth repeated term
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-satisfies = Inequality in terms of x which the number must satisfy, e.g. \`x>0\`
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-scientific = Pattern for a number in standard scientific notation
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-scientific-coefficient = Numeric value of the coefficient
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-scientific-exponent = Numeric value of the coefficient
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-scientific-numeric-value = Numeric value of this number
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-strict-order = Require terms to be in the order specified
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-subtrahend = subtrahend of the difference (b, in a-b)
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-sum = Pattern to parse sum of terms
cl-docs-description-lib-pattern-term-n = The term corresponding to argument { $termNumber } in the pattern
cl-docs-description-lib-patterns = Patterns for parsing and interpreting equations
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-point-x = Number value of x coordinate in point
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-point-y = Number value of y coordinate in point
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-equation = The equation polypad tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-geometry = The geometry polypad tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-move = The move polypad tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-none = No polypad tool is active.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-pen = The pen polypad tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tool-text = The text polypad tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-polypad-tools = Tools available in the polypad toolbar
cl-docs-description-lib-random-float =
    Member function of a random number generator. Takes a and b as inputs
    arguments, and generates an output float between a and b
cl-docs-description-lib-random-generator =
    Create a random number generator. Provide zero or more numeric arguments as
    seeds (e.g. button.pressCount) if you want the numbers from this generator to
    re-randomize when those seed values change. See further documentation below.
cl-docs-description-lib-random-int =
    Member function of a random number generator. Takes a and b as inputs
    arguments, and generates an output integer between round(a) and round(b)
    inclusive. |a| and |b| must both be less than 2^31, or the value will return
    NaN. That restriction may be relaxed in the future.
cl-docs-description-lib-replace-plus-minus =
    Takes a latex expression and a latex symbol (either + or -) and substitutes all
    the instances of \xB1 with given latex symbol.
cl-docs-description-lib-rgb = Turns three values between 0 and 255 into a rgb color. Invalid numbers become 0.
cl-docs-description-lib-set-opacity = set opacity (0 is transparent, 1 is full opacity) of a color
cl-docs-description-lib-simple-function =
    Takes a latex string and returns a function which can, for example, be passed
    into the function sink of a calculator The first argument is the latex string,
    and additional arguments are The names of the variables to treat as input
    variables (defaults to one-variable function in terms of x if not specified
cl-docs-description-lib-skech-layer = Create a layer from a sketch.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-filter-by-color =
    Filter a sketch to only the strokes and points that match the given color. Note
    that opacity does not affect this filtering.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-point-count = Takes a sketch and returns the number of points as a number.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-scale-thickness-by =
    scale the stroke thickness and point size by the provided amount,
    to a minimum of 1px for strokes and 2px for points.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-set-color = flatten all strokes and points in this sketch to the provided color
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-set-opacity =
    Change opacity of all strokes and points in the sketch to the provided alpha
    value. 0 is transparent, 1 is full opacity. Note that using \`setColor\` after
    \`setOpacity\` will override the provided alpha value
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-stroke-count = Takes a sketch and returns the number of strokes as a number.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-eraser = The eraser sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-line = The line sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-math = The math sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-pencil = The pencil sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-points = The points sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tool-text = The text sketch tool.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-tools = Tools available while sketching
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-total-stroke-length =
    Takes a sketch and returns a number the aggregate length of all strokes as a
    number.
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-transform = Apply an arbitrary transformation to a sketch, by specifying functions
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-x-values =
    Returns a numberList of all x-values that the sketch passes through at a given
    y value
cl-docs-description-lib-sketch-y-values =
    Returns a numberList of all y-values that the sketch passes through at a given
    x value
cl-docs-description-lib-slope-of-line = Returns the slope of an xyLine object.
cl-docs-description-lib-style-getter = The { $styleName } style button.
cl-docs-description-lib-substitute-latex =
    Takes a latex string, a search string, and a replace string - and returns the
    latex having made the substitution.
cl-docs-description-lib-vertex-of-parabola = Vertex of parabola.
cl-docs-description-lib-x-intercept-of-line = Returns the x-intercept of an xyLine object.
cl-docs-description-lib-x-intercept-of-parabola = X intercept(s) of parabola.
cl-docs-description-lib-xy-line = Create a new xyLine object from the provided latex string.
cl-docs-description-lib-y-intercept-of-line = Returns the y-intercept of an xyLine object.
cl-docs-description-lib-y-intercept-of-parabola = Y intercept(s) of parabola.
cl-docs-description-mc-choice-content =
    Sets the content for a given multiple choice option, indexed starting with 1.
    (This only works if the multiple choice option at this index includes some
    content already.)
cl-docs-description-mc-choice-content-source = Gets the string content for choice with the provided index.
cl-docs-description-mc-choice-location = Gets the location for choice with the provided index; to be used for rendering an annotation.
cl-docs-description-mc-disable-change = When true, disable selecting a choice or changing an existing selection.
cl-docs-description-mc-explain-content = Content of the "explain" text box.
cl-docs-description-mc-explain-prompt =
    Sets a string that replaces the generic "Explain your thinking" prompt on
    "explain" multiple choice components.
cl-docs-description-mc-initial-selection = Sets choice options as selected by default, indexed starting with 1.
cl-docs-description-mc-initial-text = Sets the initial value of the text input for explain type multiple choice.
cl-docs-description-mc-is-selected =
    Gets a Boolean that describes whether or not a particular multiple choice
    option has been selected, given the index of that option, starting with 1. This
    works for explain, simple, or multi-select multiple choice components.
cl-docs-description-mc-max-buttons-per-row =
    Takes a number from 1 to 10, and updates the layout to not allow more than that many
    buttons in a row. Note that built-in wrapping behavior could result in fewer buttons in a row.
    Only works with the "Button" layout of multiple choice or checkboxes, and only allows integer values between
    1 and 10. Values less than 1 are ignored, and values greater than 10 are clamped to 10. Non-integers are first rounded.
cl-docs-description-mc-max-selected-choices = Sets how many choices a student is allowed to select. Only applies to Checkbox components.
cl-docs-description-mc-multi-select-heading =
    Sets the prompt at the beginning of multiSelect. If blank, no prompt will show
    up. If this sink is unused, we'll use the default text: "(Select all that
    apply)"
cl-docs-description-mc-prompt =
    Sets the small italicized prompt above the choices. If blank, no prompt will
    show up. If this sink is unused and the choice type is multi-select, we will
    use the default text: "(Select all that apply.)"
cl-docs-description-mc-show-submit =
    When true, force show submit button. When false, force hide submit button,
    unless a source relies on it.
cl-docs-description-mc-submit-count = Gets the number of times the multiple choice component has been submitted.
cl-docs-description-mc-submit-label = Specify a label for the submit button.
cl-docs-description-mc-submitted =
    Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the multiple choice
    component has been submitted.
cl-docs-description-mc-time-since-submit = Gets the seconds (plus milliseconds) since the "Submit" button was pressed.
cl-docs-description-mc-wots = Configure WOSS as WOTS for teachers in PD activities
cl-docs-description-note-content =
    Sets the content of a note, which is very useful for creating dynamic elements
    in the note. This also overwrites any text you enter in the note itself. (We
    will still display text written in the note component in the teacher dashboard,
    in the thumbnail, and in the teacher guide.)
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-index-of-item =
    Returns the sorted index of the item that started with the given index (indexed
    starting with 1).
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-initial-order =
    Takes a numberList of where each item should start. Accepts any numberList as
    an order (with ties leaving two items in order). For example, [3, 1, 2] would mean that
    the first authored item would go in the last slot, the 2nd in the first slot, and the 3rd
    in the middle slot. [.25, 0, .25] would mean that the 2nd item goes first, the
    1st goes right after, and the 3rd stays 3rd. As soon as a student reorders, the
    response is locked in and this sink is ignored.
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-item-at-index =
    Returns the starting item index of the item that's at the given index (indexed
    starting with 1).
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-item-content =
    Sets the content for a given item, indexed starting with 1. (This only works if
    the item at this index exists.)
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-matches-key = Returns whether this matches the key (if provided).
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-order = Returns a numberList of where each item currently is (indexOfItem).
cl-docs-description-ordered-list-text-at-index =
    Returns the string for the item that's at the given index (indexed starting
    with 1).
cl-docs-description-penny-widget-count = Gets the number of pennies currently in the penny dragger circle.
cl-docs-description-penny-widget-size = Gets the diameter (in inches) of the current penny dragger circle.
cl-docs-description-polypad-initial-state = Sets the initial Polypad state. This will not affect the customization options in the settings menu.
cl-docs-description-polypad-initial-tool = Sets the starting tool.
cl-docs-description-polypad-is-initial-state-source = Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether the student has interacted with the Polypad.
cl-docs-description-polypad-narration =
    Text that screen readers will read aloud. Similar to image alt text, narration can be used to describe a polypad.
    As with the graph narration sink, you can include multiple narrations for a polypad to separate pieces of
    information from one another.  This allows you to modify narrations independently and minimizes the amount of
    text a screen reader needs to speak.
cl-docs-description-polypad-state-source = Gets the full state of a Polypad. Pass this, for example, into the Polypad's initialState sink.
cl-docs-description-polypad-tile-location = Gets the location of a Polypad tile; to be used for rendering an annotation.
cl-docs-description-polypad-value-source = Gets an exported value from a Validation Tile on a Polypad.
cl-docs-description-reset-animation-on-change = Specify a string value. If that value changes, the animation timer resets.
cl-docs-description-reset-on-change = Specify a string value. If that value changes, the component resets.
cl-docs-description-sketch-allow-eraser =
    Sometimes you only want students to be able to clear, not erase. Set this to
    false if that's the mood you're in.
cl-docs-description-sketch-audiotrace-reverse =
    If the sketch has a graph background, specifies whether expressions are
    traversed in reverse order when audio trace is active. This behavior may be
    desired in situations where the curves you wish a student to examine are
    declared at the end of the calculator's expression list so that they appear in
    the foreground.
cl-docs-description-sketch-available-colors = Configures the available colors in sketch.
cl-docs-description-sketch-background = Sets the background of the sketch.
cl-docs-description-sketch-bounds-sink =
    Sets the bounds of this sketch. If the sketch has a graph background, it will
    be updated to match.
cl-docs-description-sketch-bounds-source = Gets the bounds of a sketch component.
cl-docs-description-sketch-current-stroke = Gets a sketch object that represents the current stroke in progress.
cl-docs-description-sketch-current-x =
    Gets the current x-coordinate of the mouse. Works on hover with a mouse and
    while depressed for touch.
cl-docs-description-sketch-current-y =
    Gets the current y-coordinate of the mouse. Works on hover with a mouse and
    while depressed for touch.
cl-docs-description-sketch-disable-sketch = Sets whether drawing on a sketch is permitted.
cl-docs-description-sketch-expression-sink =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets a variable in the calculator to
    an expression with the provided latex.
    This will override any existing definitions of that variable. The first parameter
    is the name of the variable or function to be defined. The optional additional parameters
    specify the symbols that the latex expression is allowed to reference. (By default,
    it will not be allowed to reference any existing variables or functions in the calculator.)
cl-docs-description-sketch-hide-sketch =
    Hides the student's sketch. Also disables sketching since anything sketched
    would be hidden.
cl-docs-description-sketch-initial-color = Sets the starting color.
cl-docs-description-sketch-initial-tool = Sets the starting tool.
cl-docs-description-sketch-label-latex =
    If the sketch has a graph background, gets the inner latex content from a point
    label in the graph based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-sketch-label-numeric-value =
    If the sketch has a graph background, evaluates the content of a point label in
    the graph based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-sketch-label-text =
    If the sketch has a graph background, gets the text content from a point label
    in the graph based on the name of the point.
cl-docs-description-sketch-number-list-sink =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets a variable in the calculator to the
    contents of a list. This will override any existing definitions of that
    variable.
cl-docs-description-sketch-number-list-source =
    If the sketch has a graph background, gets the list of numbers that was
    assigned to the variable in the graph.
cl-docs-description-sketch-number-sink =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets the value of a variable in the
    calculator. This will override any existing definitions of that variable.
cl-docs-description-sketch-number-source =
    If the sketch has a graph background, gets the numerical value of a variable in
    the graph.
cl-docs-description-sketch-object = Gets a sketch object that represents everything drawn on the sketch.
cl-docs-description-sketch-point-location =
    If the sketch has a graph background, gets a location for a point to be used with feedback annotations.
    This takes a point name as the first argument and optional width and height arguments (in math space).
    If no width or height params then a default location size will be used and if only a
    width is supplied then the height will be set to the supplied width.
cl-docs-description-sketch-raw-expression-point-label =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets a label for a point on the graph.
    This only works for points defined like A=(1,2), and the identifier needs to
    match the name given to the point (A in this case). Takes a string. The label
    next to the point exactly matches the provided string, so the label is turned
    off if the empty string is provided.
cl-docs-description-sketch-smart-stroke-joining =
    Perform mutations on mouseup: removing nearby points and joining with other
    strokes. Most useful when sketch is used for curve sketching, e.g. in
    Function Carnival. Defaults to false.
cl-docs-description-sketch-trace =
    If the sketch has a graph background, allows tracing curves to inspect
    coordinates and shows point coordinates when clicked.
cl-docs-description-sketch-x-axis-label =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets the string we display along the
    x-axis.
cl-docs-description-sketch-y-axis-label =
    If the sketch has a graph background, sets the string we display along the
    y-axis.
cl-docs-description-step-cover-button-label =
    Use in conjunction with coverText to change the button text from the default ("Ok").
    If set to an empty string, the cover won't be dismissable.
cl-docs-description-step-cover-text = Covers the screen with the text provided. The cover is dismissable.
cl-docs-description-step-disable-calculator-reason = If provided, disables the calculator tool.
cl-docs-description-step-disable-sketch-everywhere = Disable sketch everywhere toolbar.
cl-docs-description-step-export = Data to include in CSV export to summarize this screen.
cl-docs-description-step-play-feedback = Triggers annotated feedback playback if set to the name of an item of feedback authored for this screen.
cl-docs-description-step-subtitle = Adds a subtitle that is centered under the screen title.
cl-docs-description-step-title =
    Overrides the provided title with a string value. You can use string
    interpolation (e.g., "hello { "\${ name }" }") and conditionals to build rich text to
    show to the user. Note: We recommend including placeholder text as the display
    content, which will appear in the miniscreen, teacher dashboard, and teacher
    guide.
cl-docs-description-table-capture = Specify a number to capture. Retrieve all such numbers with the history source.
cl-docs-description-table-cell-content-sink =
    Sets the contents of a cell given the row index and column index of the cell.
    (Row index 1 is the first row underneath the header.)
cl-docs-description-table-cell-content-source =
    Gets the contents of a cell given a row index and column index. (Row index 1
    is the first row underneath the header.)
cl-docs-description-table-cell-disable-evaluation =
    Disable the evaluation of math typed by the student in this cell. Only affects
    cells in math type columns.
cl-docs-description-table-cell-editable =
    Overrides all other mechanisms of deciding whether the student can edit this
    cell.
cl-docs-description-table-cell-error-message =
    An error to show to the student. Note: This will not show up in the teacher
    dashboard. (Use the "warning" sink to show warnings to the teacher.)
cl-docs-description-table-cell-has-focus =
    Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the student is editing a
    cell given the row index and column index of the cell. (Row index 1 is the
    first row underneath the header.)
cl-docs-description-table-cell-location = Gets the location of a table cell given the row index and column index; to be used for rendering an annotation.
cl-docs-description-table-cell-numeric-value =
    Gets the evaluated numeric value of that cell given a row index and column
    index. (Row index 1 is the first row underneath the header.) If a student types
    "2 + 2", we will return "4".
cl-docs-description-table-cell-suffix =
    Adds a suffix to everything entered by the student. Recommended for inputs that
    expect a certain unit (e.g., ft. or %). Only shows up for
    expression types of cells.
cl-docs-description-table-column-numeric-value =
    Gets the evaluated contents of each cell in a column and returns it as a number
    list given the column's index.
cl-docs-description-table-disable-row-changes =
    Sets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the student can add or
    remove rows. Similar to fill-in-the-blank mode, but allows for existing cells
    to be edited. Highly recommended for use with any cell specific sources.
    (e.g., cellContent or cellNumericValue.)
cl-docs-description-table-initial-cell-content =
    Sets the initial value of the cell at the row index and column index provided.
    This will unlock the cell and students can override the initial value. Note:
    Should be a valid latex string if setting for a math type of cell (default).
cl-docs-description-table-max-rows = Sets the number of rows the table will display.
cl-docs-description-table-submit-button-disabled = Must be used in conjunction with submitButtonText. Disables the submit button.
cl-docs-description-table-submit-button-text =
    When set, adds a submit button with this text. Gives a timeSinceSubmit and
    submitted source. Resets automatically if the student focuses back into the
    table.
cl-docs-description-table-submitted =
    Gets a Boolean value that indicates whether or not the table component has been
    submitted.
cl-docs-description-table-time-since-submit = Gets the seconds (plus milliseconds) since the "Submit" button was pressed.
cl-docs-description-text-input-content = Gets the student input value as a string.
cl-docs-description-text-input-initial-text = Sets the initial value of the text input.
cl-docs-description-text-input-placeholder-text = Sets the placeholder text of the input.
cl-docs-description-text-input-show-submit =
    When true, force show submit button. When false, force hide submit button,
    unless a source relies on it.
cl-docs-description-text-input-submit-label = Specify a label for the submit button.
cl-docs-description-text-input-submitted = Gets a Boolean value indicating whether or not the input has been submitted.
cl-docs-description-text-input-time-since-submit = Gets the seconds (plus milliseconds) since the submit button was pressed.
cl-docs-description-text-input-wots = Configure WOSS as WOTS for teachers in PD activities
cl-docs-description-transform-read-only =
    Sets a Boolean value that determines whether or not a component will be ignored
    when determining a screen's correctness. If all components have a readOnly
    value of "true," we display a dash for the student's screen in the dashboard's
    summary view, indicating teachers can focus their efforts elsewhere.
cl-docs-description-type-bounds = Represents the mathematical bounds of a graph or sketch.
cl-docs-description-type-button-styles = Contains the Desmos button styles.
cl-docs-description-type-color = Represents a color.
cl-docs-description-type-color-palette = Contains the Desmos colors.
cl-docs-description-type-conic = Represents a conic section.
cl-docs-description-type-equation = Represents a mathematical equation.
cl-docs-description-type-evaluation-frame = A frame object to store functions and variables for future evaluation.
cl-docs-description-type-inequality = Represents a mathematical inequality.
cl-docs-description-type-list = Represents a list of items.
cl-docs-description-type-math-expression = Represents a mathematical function that can be evaluated.
cl-docs-description-type-ordered-pair = Represents an ordered pair.
cl-docs-description-type-parabola = Represents a parabola.
cl-docs-description-type-polypad-point = Represents a 2-D point in a Polypad coordinate system.
cl-docs-description-type-polypad-tools = Contains the tools from the polypad component toolbar.
cl-docs-description-type-random-generator = Contains random number generators.
cl-docs-description-type-sketch = Represents the data for a sketch.
cl-docs-description-type-sketch-tools = Contains the tools from the sketch component toolbar.
cl-docs-description-type-xy-line = Represents a linear equation or expression.
cl-docs-description-video-time-sink = Sets the playhead time of the video (seconds).
cl-docs-description-video-time-source = Gets the current playhead time of the video (seconds).
cl-docs-heading-component-sinks = Sinks:
cl-docs-heading-component-sources = Sources:
cl-docs-heading-component-sources-sample-code = Sample Code:
cl-docs-heading-functions-table = Functions:
cl-docs-heading-overview = Overview
cl-docs-heading-sinks = sinks
cl-docs-heading-sources = sources
cl-docs-heading-type-attributes = Attributes:
cl-docs-label-deprecated = deprecated
cl-docs-label-internal = internal
cl-docs-label-navigation-next = Next Up: { $sectionName }
cl-docs-label-no-sample = No code sample available
cl-docs-label-no-sinks = no sinks
cl-docs-label-no-sources = no sources
cl-docs-label-sample-loading = Loading code sample.
cl-docs-label-search-count = Results
cl-docs-label-sink-count = { $count } sinks
cl-docs-label-sink-count-single = 1 sink
cl-docs-label-source-count = { $count } sources
cl-docs-label-source-count-single = 1 source
cl-docs-label-step-sources = Sources
cl-docs-message-complete-prop = Access the variables defined in this component.
cl-docs-message-empty-search = Try searching for components, sinks, or sources.
cl-docs-message-mc-multi-select-heading-deprecation = Use prompt instead.
cl-docs-narration-close-sidebar = Close Sidebar
cl-docs-narration-open-sidebar = Open Sidebar
cl-docs-placeholder-searchbox = Search CL documentation
cl-docs-title-cl-playground = Computation Layer Playground
cl-docs-title-component-graph = Graph and Graphing Calc
cl-docs-title-component-mc = Multiple Choice and Checkboxes
cl-docs-title-main = Computation Layer Documentation
cl-docs-title-section-advanced = Advanced
cl-docs-title-section-aggregate = Aggregate
cl-docs-title-section-component = { $componentName } Component
cl-docs-title-section-components = Components
cl-docs-title-section-conditionals = Conditionals
cl-docs-title-section-correctness = Correctness
cl-docs-title-section-deprecated-functions = Deprecated Functions
cl-docs-title-section-dynamic-text = Dynamic Text
cl-docs-title-section-getting-started = Getting Started
cl-docs-title-section-graphs-sketches = Graphs and Sketches
cl-docs-title-section-interpreting-math = Interpreting Math
cl-docs-title-section-logic-and-conditionals = Logic and Conditionals
cl-docs-title-section-other-functions = Other Functions
cl-docs-title-section-patterns = Patterns
cl-docs-title-section-random = Random Numbers
cl-docs-title-section-screen = Screen
cl-docs-title-section-sinks-sources = Sinks and Sources
cl-docs-title-section-types = Types
cl-docs-title-section-welcome = Welcome
cl-docs-title-short = Computation Layer Docs
cl-docs-warning-bounds-strategy-deprecation-notice = Please use bounds.METHODNAME instead.
cl-docs-warning-deprecation-angle-of-line = Please use line.angle instead.
cl-docs-warning-deprecation-is-line-horizontal = Please use line.isHorizontal instead.
